cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or benchmark in research, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "Adaptive Urban Navigation with Reinforcement Learning under Route Disruptions"
authors:
  - given-names: Mohamad
    family-names: Shamsi Jazeb
abstract: >
  A small reproducible reinforcement-learning benchmark for deterministic grid
  navigation under an unexpected route disruption. The repository includes
  tabular Q-learning and a compact DQN baseline, with evaluation separating
  immediate post-disruption robustness from continued-learning recovery.
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohamad679/adaptive-urban-navigation-rl"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - adaptive navigation
  - route disruption
  - Q-learning
  - DQN
  - reproducible research
